### Task Model

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|-----------|--------------|--------------|------------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1** | Estimate Waiting Time | AND | Storage | 1 | The robot performs a query on the queue length at each storage; only one robot is needed. |
| **AT2** | Estimate Path | AND | Storage | 1 | The robot computes the travel distance to each storage; only one robot is needed. |
| **AT3** | Request Resources from Storage | AND | Storage | 1 | Sending a request message is performed by the robot that will collect the resources. |
| **AT4** | Wait for Retrieval | AND | Storage | 1 | The robot waits until the storage confirms that the resources have been retrieved. |
| **AT5** | Check Battery Level during Collection | AND | Robot’s Current Location | 1 | Battery monitoring is performed by the robot itself. |
| **AT6** | Handle Low Battery during Collection | AND | Recharging Station | 1 | When battery <10 % the robot must return to recharge and hand over the mission to another robot. |
| **AT7** | Move Resources to Destination | AND | Requesting Agent’s Location | 1 | The robot physically transports the resources to the requested location. |
| **AT8** | Check Battery Level during Delivery | AND | Robot’s Current Location | 1 | Battery monitoring is performed by the robot itself. |
| **AT9** | Return Resource to Checkpoint and Assign Remaining Task | AND | Checkpoint | 1 | If battery <30 % the robot must drop the resource at a checkpoint and hand over the remaining delivery to another robot that knows the checkpoint location. |
| **AT10** | Trigger Alert and Report to Sector Manager | AND | Recharging Station / Robot’s Current Location | 1 | Failure to return to a checkpoint triggers an alert and a report to the sector manager. |
| **AT11** | Assign Multiple Robots for Parallel Collect‑Deliver Tasks | AND | Robot Coordination Hub | [2,∞] | The mission may need two or more robots to handle multiple items concurrently, as stated in the description. |
| **AT12** | Manage Task Assignment to Reduce Time | AND | Robot Coordination Hub | 1 | The robot coordination hub optimizes the assignment of remaining tasks to other robots after a low‑battery event. |

